   $q$Read: "A tree adds one new ring to its trunk every year. In years with plenty of rain, the ring is wide. In dry years, the ring is thin." Which sentence would best conclude this paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By reading the rings, scientists can learn a tree's age and the weather it lived through.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In dry years, the new ring is very thin.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-detail"},{"text":"Forests cover large parts of many different countries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"Some trees have leaves that turn bright orange in the fall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-conclusion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By reading the rings, scientists can learn a tree's age and the weather it lived through.$q$, $q$The paragraph explains that rings show each year and its rainfall, so a sentence about learning age and weather from rings sums it up. Repeating that dry years make thin rings only restates the last detail without concluding.$q$, 'draft', null)
