   $q$Read the paragraph: (A) People have flown kites for more than two thousand years. (B) Long ago, some kites were used to send signals across long distances. (C) Later, scientists tied instruments to kites to measure wind and temperature high in the air. (D) My uncle flies a kite at the beach every summer. Which sentence does not belong?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence D","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence B","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-topic-sentence"},{"text":"Sentence C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence D$q$, $q$The paragraph is about how kites have been used throughout history, and an uncle's beach trips are a personal detail that does not fit. Sentence C belongs because "Later" continues the history that sentence B begins.$q$, 'draft', null)
