   $q$Read the sentences: (A) After the walks, they refilled every water bowl. (B) When the volunteers arrived at the animal shelter, they signed in at the front desk. (C) By the end of the day, every dog had been walked and fed. (D) Then each volunteer took two dogs out for a walk. Which is the most logical order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"D, B, A, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"B, A, D, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"B, D, A, C","is_correct":true},{"text":"B, D, C, A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-closing-cue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, D, A, C$q$, $q$The volunteers sign in when they arrive, then walk the dogs, then refill bowls "after the walks," and "By the end of the day" wraps it up. Order B, A, D, C is wrong because sentence A says the walks are over before sentence D describes them starting.$q$, 'draft', null)
