  ('a99e4aae-479a-51fd-927f-bcf047eca2da', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$A paragraph ends: "Folding paper cranes helped our class practice measuring angles and finding lines of symmetry." The next paragraph describes how engineers use paper folding to design solar panels that fold up for space travel. Which sentence would best begin the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In conclusion, paper folding is a fun hobby.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conclusion-for-transition"},{"text":"Paper folding is useful far beyond a math classroom, too.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A paper crane needs about twenty separate folds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-first-paragraph"},{"text":"For example, our class also folded paper frogs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-for-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Paper folding is useful far beyond a math classroom, too.$q$, $q$This sentence links the classroom idea from the first paragraph to the new idea of paper folding outside school, which is what the engineers paragraph is about. "For example, our class also folded paper frogs" stays in the classroom, so it does not lead into the engineers.$q$, 'draft', null)
