   $q$Read the sentences: (A) This energy is stored in a small battery inside the charger. (B) A solar charger has a panel that turns sunlight into electricity. (C) Later, when you plug in a phone, the battery sends the stored energy to it. (D) Because of this design, you can charge a phone even after the sun goes down. Which is the most logical order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"B, A, C, D","is_correct":true},{"text":"B, D, A, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conclusion-too-early"},{"text":"A, B, C, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-pronoun-reference"},{"text":"B, C, A, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-pronoun-reference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, A, C, D$q$, $q$"This energy" in sentence A needs sentence B before it, sentence C uses "Later" and "the stored energy" after the battery is mentioned, and D sums up the whole design. Order A, B, C, D is wrong because "This energy" would come before any energy has been named.$q$, 'draft', null)
